      "kind": "faq",
      "heading": "Questions, answered",
      "html": "<h3>What is a commercial insurance risk survey report?</h3><p>A report that describes an insured risk so an underwriter can price it. It covers COPE (construction, occupancy, protection and exposure), the fire and security protections, and the changes you recommend. The underwriter uses it without visiting.</p><h3>What does COPE mean in an insurance survey?</h3><p>Construction, occupancy, protection and exposure. Construction is what the building is made of. Occupancy is the trade inside and its hazards. Protection is the fire and security systems. Exposure is what surrounds the site.</p><h3>Why record a risk survey on site?</h3><p>The details that move the rate fade fastest. Was the sprinkler system maintained? Did the alarm panel show a fault? A report written two days later loses them. Quickler asks in WhatsApp as you walk, so photos and answers are in the right place.</p><h3>Can I use Quickler for insurance risk survey reports?</h3><p>Yes. You answer each question by text, voice note or photo. When you say done, Quickler writes the report. You get Word, PDF or a web link. There is no new app.</p><h3>Will it match my own survey report?</h3><p>Send us a finished report of yours, in Word or PDF. Every new one comes back in that layout. You still read it and sign it. It is not underwriting or legal advice.</p><h3>Related guides</h3><ul><li><a href=\"/pages/insurance-survey-software-uk.html\">Insurance survey software (overview)</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/property-risk-assessment-insurance-uk.html\">Property risk assessment for insurers</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/fire-risk-assessment-insurance-uk.html\">Fire risk assessment survey app</a></li><li><a href=\"/pages/loss-adjuster-site-report-app-uk.html\">Loss adjuster site report app</a></li></ul>"
